  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "I fixed the shared parser state machine. Changes were confined to the two writable files.\n\n**`src/state.mjs`** (the core fix):\n- **CRLF across chunks**: a CR outside quotes now sets `pendingCR` and returns without ending the record. The next character must be LF (then the record ends) or a `BARE_CR` `SyntaxError` is thrown. This makes `['a,one\\r', '\\nb,two']` and `['a,one\\r\\nb,two']` identical, and a trailing CR at end of input raises `BARE_CR` via `finishState`.\n- **Doubled quotes across chunks**: in `afterQuote`, a second `\"` now appends one literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode (previously it threw `INVALID_QUOTE`). So `\"\"` split across chunks unescapes correctly, and a closing quote followed by comma/CR/LF/EOF is handled.\n- **Closing quote followed by CR**: enters `pendingCR` so CRLF after a quoted field is validated the same way as elsewhere.\n- **Record ending** is centralized in `endRecord`, which finishes the field, pushes the record, and resets `mode`/`atFieldStart`/`pendingCR`, so state is consistent regardless of where chunks split.\n- `finishState` still reports `BARE_CR` before `UNTERMINATED_QUOTE`, and only emits a final record when something was touched, so empty input yields `[]` and a trailing line ending adds no extra row.\n\n**`src/line.mjs`**: `consumeLine` no longer treats a bare CR as a record terminator; it just ends the record and resets state, with CR/LF validation owned by the caller. (It is no longer imported by `state.mjs`, but is now consistent with the grammar.)\n\nUnchanged: `src/index.mjs` exports, `tokenizer.mjs`, the consumers, `item-schema.mjs`, `escape.mjs`, `assembler.mjs`, and the slug/checksum helpers.\n\n**What was checked**: I re-read both edited files to confirm the final content. I did not run any tests — no shell or test execution is available in this environment, so I cannot claim the public tests pass.",
